%N A400963 Decimal expansion of the real solution to x^5 - 5*x^4 - 10*x^3 - 10*x^2 - 5*x - 1 = 0.
%C A400963 An equation 2*x^n - (x+1)^n = 0 (including this one) has positive real solution 1 / (2^(1/n) - 1). If n is even, the equation also has a negative real solution -1 / (2^(1/n) + 1). If n is greater than 2, the remaining solutions are complex numbers in the form 1 / (r * 2^(1/n) - 1) where r are nonreal n-th roots of unity.
%C A400963 Absolute values of the coefficients of the polynomial in such equation form the n-th row of Pascal's triangle (A007318). In this case, 1, 5, 10, 10, 5, 1 are the numbers from the 5th row of Pascal's triangle.
%C A400963 This constant is a Pisot-Vijayaraghavan number.
%H A400963 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_05">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 5</a>.
%F A400963 Equals 1 / (2^(1/5) - 1).
%F A400963 Equals 1 + 2^(1/5) + 4^(1/5) + 8^(1/5) + 16^(1/5) = 1 + A005531 + A005533 + A011093 + A011101.
%e A400963 6.7250239588725756...
%p A400963 evalf(1+2^(1/5)+4^(1/5)+8^(1/5)+16^(1/5), 105);
%t A400963 RealDigits[1/(2^(1/5) - 1), 10, 105][[1]]
%o A400963 (PARI) 1/(2^(1/5)-1)
%Y A400963 Cf. A005531, A005533, A007318, A011093, A011101.
%K A400963 nonn,cons,new
